---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    question: "Who is Onur Aksoy and what are his core domains of expertise?",
    answer: "Onur Aksoy is an Ankara-based Software Developer, Digital Strategist & Systems Architect and multidisciplinary creator (operating in the digital sphere under the subsystem moniker Hackonomist). He builds high-availability Windows desktop applications (oaPOS), progressive web2app platforms (Orvyna App Studio), in-browser FFmpeg WASM video splitter extension on Microsoft Edge Add-ons (10SeC), technical SEO tooling (SEO Lens), generative computer vision engines, and integrates digital growth strategies with full-stack software development."
  },
  {
    question: "What does the moniker Hackonomist represent?",
    answer: "Hackonomist is the established professional moniker and subsystem identity of Onur Aksoy. It symbolizes the intersection of system 'hacking' (software architecture, automation, reverse-engineering, deterministic algorithms) and 'economics' (incentive design, growth hacking, market conversion, and unit economics). In search engines and AI knowledge graphs, 'Hackonomist' refers exclusively to Onur Aksoy."
  },
  {
    question: "What is the difference between an AI-driven and AI-native developer?",
    answer: "While an AI-driven developer uses AI merely as an autocomplete or coding assistant, an AI-native developer architects systems from the ground up where autonomous AI agents, deterministic state machines, and LLM context graphs act as core production partners. Onur designs software with strict typing, deterministic boundaries, and automated multi-agent verification."
  },
  {
    question: "What core technical services and architectural solutions does Onur Aksoy provide?",
    answer: "Onur Aksoy specializes in four core disciplines: (1) AI-Native Software & Agentic Automation, (2) Local-First Windows Desktop POS & Inventory Systems, (3) Direct Store Web2App Packaging (Apple TestFlight & Google Play TWA), and (4) Multidisciplinary Creative Production (Video, Audio, Performance Advertising, and Growth Strategy)."
  },
  {
    question: "How does the oaPOS HOST/CLIENT architecture maintain offline resilience?",
    answer: "oaPOS uses a local-first peer architecture connecting multiple POS and barcode terminals over local area network (LAN) raw TCP/IP sockets without relying on external cloud servers or internet connectivity. Data synchronizes across devices with sub-10ms latency directly on modern embedded SQLite and distributed datastores."
  },
  {
    question: "What is Orvyna App Studio?",
    answer: "Orvyna App Studio is an automated web2app compilation platform created by Onur Aksoy. It inspects responsive web applications, extracts metadata and icons, and delivers direct Apple TestFlight / App Store Connect delivery and Google Play TWA/AAB packages with sub-150KB shell footprints in under 3 seconds."
  },
  {
    question: "How does Onur Aksoy bridge marketing, video production, and software development?",
    answer: "Rather than treating code, content, and marketing as isolated silos, Onur unites them into a single product-focused workflow: from market research and conversion-optimized software architecture to studio video shooting, creative ad campaigns, and SEO/GEO generative search discovery."
  },
  {
    question: "How can clients hire or collaborate with Onur Aksoy?",
    answer: "Onur Aksoy is available for strategic consulting, high-impact software development, and enterprise architecture advisory. Clients can reach him directly at dev@onuraksoy.com.tr, or via Telegram (@oaonuraksoy) and WhatsApp (+905511817053)."
  }
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Onur Aksoy — Software Developer, Digital Strategist & Systems Architect"
  description="Editorial biography, architectural convictions, and background of Onur Aksoy. Pioneering deterministic AI systems and local-first software development."
  lang="en"
  activeNav="about"
  schemaType="Person"
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 py-16">
    <!-- Header with Color Portrait -->
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center md:items-start gap-8 pb-12 border-b border-obsidian-border mb-12">
      <div class="relative w-44 sm:w-52 aspect-[4/5] rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-gold-tungsten/40 shadow-xl flex-shrink-0 bg-obsidian-surface">
        <img
          src="/images/onur-aksoy.webp"
          alt="Onur Aksoy — Software Developer, Digital Strategist & Systems Architect"
          class="w-full h-full object-cover object-top scale-100 hover:scale-105 transition-all duration-700"
          width="937"
          height="1679"
          fetchpriority="high"
          loading="eager"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </div>

      <div>
        <span class="text-xs font-mono tracking-widest text-gold-tungsten uppercase font-semibold">
          Biography & Manifesto
        </span>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-text-primary mt-1 mb-3">
          Onur Aksoy
        </h1>
        <p class="text-base text-gold-highlight font-medium mb-4">
          Software Developer, Digital Strategist & Systems Architect (a.k.a. Hackonomist)
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed max-w-xl">
          Based in Ankara, Turkey, operating at the intersection of high-availability desktop software development, deterministic artificial intelligence architectures, and multidisciplinary digital design.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Architectural Convictions -->
    <section class="space-y-10 text-text-muted leading-relaxed">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-gold-tungsten"></span>
          The Philosophy: Determinism Over Hallucination
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          The dominant trend in artificial intelligence software often favors flashy conversational wrappers that mask erratic non-deterministic failures behind polite apologies. My approach is strictly rooted in architectural discipline:
        </p>
        <p class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-obsidian-surface border-l-2 border-gold-tungsten text-sm text-text-primary italic">
          "State machines must remain mathematically deterministic, schemas must be strictly enforced, and generative AI agents must operate under multi-layered audit loops."
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-gold-tungsten"></span>
          Local-First Software Sovereignty
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          In an era where every utility demands a monthly cloud subscription and risks operational shutdown whenever network connections glitch, I build systems that prioritize local data sovereignty.
        </p>
        <p>
          Whether building enterprise point-of-sale platforms like <strong class="text-text-primary">oaPOS</strong> with local socket LAN synchronization, or crafting lightweight containerized web wrappers with <strong class="text-text-primary">Orvyna App Studio</strong>, the goal remains the same: microsecond performance, zero operational rents, and continuous autonomy.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Core Technical Arsenal -->
      <div class="pt-6 border-t border-obsidian-border">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-6">
          Technical Arsenal & Core Stack
        </h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-xs font-mono">
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-obsidian-surface border border-obsidian-border">
            <span class="text-gold-highlight font-bold block mb-2">Systems & Desktop</span>
            <ul class="space-y-1 text-text-muted">
              <li>• .NET 8 / C# / WPF / XAML</li>
              <li>• SQLite / Embedded Databases</li>
              <li>• Asynchronous TCP/IP LAN Sockets</li>
              <li>• ESC/POS Thermal Printing Engines</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-obsidian-surface border border-obsidian-border">
            <span class="text-gold-highlight font-bold block mb-2">AI & Generative Pipelines</span>
            <ul class="space-y-1 text-text-muted">
              <li>• Autonomous Subagent Orchestration</li>
              <li>• Latent Diffusion & Inpainting Pipelines</li>
              <li>• Sub-pixel Edge Alpha Matting</li>
              <li>• Schema.org & GEO Knowledge Engines</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-obsidian-surface border border-obsidian-border">
            <span class="text-gold-highlight font-bold block mb-2">Modern Web & Containers</span>
            <ul class="space-y-1 text-text-muted">
              <li>• Astro 7 / Content Layer / Zero-JS</li>
              <li>• TypeScript / Vite / Web Components</li>
              <li>• Store Web2App (TestFlight & TWA)</li>
              <li>• Workbox Caching Architectures</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-obsidian-surface border border-obsidian-border">
            <span class="text-gold-highlight font-bold block mb-2">Creative & Audio Production</span>
            <ul class="space-y-1 text-text-muted">
              <li>• Podcasting & Editorial Broadcasts</li>
              <li>• Sound Design & Audio Production</li>
              <li>• Obsidian/Tungsten Visual Direction</li>
              <li>• Vector Typography & Brand Assets</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Podcast Note -->
      <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-obsidian-surface border border-obsidian-border flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-6">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-text-primary">
            Merhaba Dünya, Ben Onur Aksoy
          </h3>
          <p class="text-xs text-text-muted mt-1">
            Spotify Podcast (a.k.a. Hackonomist) — Deep reflections on technology, systems architecture, and independent product building.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a
          href="https://open.spotify.com/show/3FSqxgXs900CueJqIJwUQA"
          target="_blank"
          rel="me noopener noreferrer"
          class="flex-shrink-0 px-4 py-2 rounded-lg bg-emerald-950 text-emerald-300 border border-emerald-800 text-xs font-semibold hover:bg-emerald-900 transition-colors"
        >
          Stream on Spotify ↗
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Verified Entity & Knowledge Graph Records -->
